{"title":"Career roadmap · ERP Executive","role":"ERP Executive","summary":"An ERP Executive supports the implementation, configuration, administration and day-to-day operation of enterprise resource planning systems. The role connects business processes with technology, covering areas such as finance, procurement, inventory, sales, HR and operations.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Com (Bachelor of Commerce)","Course":"B.Com – Computer Applications"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"B.Com – Computer Applications is strongly aligned because it combines commerce/accounting knowledge with computer applications, making it suitable for ERP functional and business-process roles."},{"type":"note","label":"Career-route check","text":"Direct alignment. A strong route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Com Computer Applications","ERP/Business Applications Intern","ERP Executive","ERP Functional Consultant","Senior Consultant/ERP Lead"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career objective"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build accounting, business-process, SQL, ERP and Excel skills; enter as ERP Executive/ERP Support Associate"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in SAP, Oracle, Microsoft Dynamics or another ERP platform and become a functional consultant"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Lead ERP modules, implementations, integrations and business-process transformation"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward ERP Solution Architect, Enterprise Applications Manager, ERP Programme Manager or Digital Transformation leadership"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Commerce + accounting fundamentals"},{"text":"Financial accounting, business processes"},{